# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What must NOT get in matters more than what is missing. Two kinds:
#   1. ROM data in any form: the source, a generated VHDL table, a compiled simulation.
#      The source alone being excluded is not enough, what is generated from it must be
#      excluded too.
#   2. Credentials and built firmware.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- ROM data, never in the repository ---
# the folder itself is in the repository (with its README), its contents are not
roms/*
!roms/README.md
# ... also when it ends up outside roms/ (every zip is caught further down)
*.rom
# generated tables and their compiled form: make_rom.py and build.tcl write into gen/
**/proms/*.vhd
**/work/
**/gen/
**/frames/

# --- RetroAchievements data and ROM names, never in the repository ---
# Sets and code notes belong to RetroAchievements, the card files of the client carry the
# account's state, the other names are ROM sets. scripts/checks.sh refuses a staged or pushed
# file that matches this list, git add -f included.
gg1_*
prom-*
*.zip
*.7z
ra_patch.json
ra_patch.mac
ra_unlocked.txt
ra_pending.txt
ra_parked.txt
patch_[0-9]*.json
codenotes*.json

# --- credentials ---
# They live in sdcard/config.ini, excluded below. Nothing here uses .env files, this line is
# a precaution in case one ever appears.
*.env

# --- Gowin build output ---
impl/
*.fs
*.bin
*.bit
*.log
# each core's packed menu, scripts/make_menu.py writes it at every build
menu_xml.hex

# --- Pico build output ---
build/
build_*/
# A built firmware carries BTstack with its non-commercial clause: redistribution only with
# the licence notice. Build output anyway, not versioned.
*.uf2
*.elf

# --- release output of scripts/make_firmware_release.sh, published on the release page ---
dist/

# --- third-party repositories under external/ ---
# FPGA-Companion, pico-sdk, tinyusb and unity are git submodules and therefore tracked. The SDK
# caches picotool there (picotool-src), that stays untracked.
external/*
!external/FPGA-Companion
!external/pico-sdk
!external/tinyusb
!external/unity

# --- macOS ---
.DS_Store

# --- Python caches ---
__pycache__/

# --- example card: the generated file carries secrets, the game files name the ROMs ---
sdcard/config.ini
sdcard/*.ini
